# The level-M modular function algebra is a domain

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.LevelN.isDomain_ring` (`fccdc20b-3a1a-5bc6-a90b-d25f25b7fb94`), by
Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `1f2d0570-7bf2-5618-a906-add1a8ff3677`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Fix a natural number $M \neq 0$. Inside the commutative $\mathbb{C}$-algebra of all functions
$\mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ with pointwise operations, consider the $\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra
[`ModularCurve.LevelN.ring M`](def/ModularCurve_LevelNFunctionField.html#L28), defined as the
algebra generated by the set [`ModularCurve.LevelN.generators
M`](def/ModularCurve_LevelNFunctionField.html#L25), which consists of the function
[`ModularCurve.LevelN.jAnalytic`](def/ModularCurve_LevelNFunctionField.html#L22) together with all
functions of the form [`ModularCurve.LevelN.fricke M
v`](def/ModularCurve_LevelNFunctionField.html#L19) for $v \colon \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to \mathbb{Z}/M$
with $v \neq 0$; concretely, the first generator is $\tau \mapsto E_4(\tau)^3/\Delta(\tau)$, and the
generator attached to $v$ is $\tau \mapsto -\bigl(E_4(\tau)E_6(\tau)/\Delta(\tau)\bigr)/2592 \cdot
(2\pi i)^{-2}\,\wp\bigl(\tfrac{v_0\tau + v_1}{M}\bigr)$, the Weierstrass $\wp$-function being taken
for the period pair with $\omega_1 = \tau$, $\omega_2 = 1$. The assertion is that this subalgebra,
with its induced ring structure, is an integral domain: it is a nontrivial commutative ring in which
a product of two nonzero elements is nonzero.

This supplies the fact tacitly needed to speak of the function field of the modular curve of level
$M$: the ring of functions generated by $j$ and the nonzero Fricke functions has a field of
fractions, so statements about the level-$M$ function field phrased for an arbitrary fraction field
of this ring may be instantiated. It is used in the treatment of orders of vanishing and of the
$X_1$-function-field relations for coprime levels.

